@startuml Online Payment Gateway Simulation - Use Case Diagram
' Corrected version of "1. UML Use Case Diagram" image.
' Fixes: removed crossing lines, fixed <<include>> directions, scoped actors properly.
left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor "Customer\n(Payer)" as Customer
actor "Merchant\n(Business)" as Merchant
actor "Administrator" as Admin
actor "Simulated Bank /\nCard Network" as Bank
actor "Notification\nService" as Notify

rectangle "Online Payment Gateway Simulation" {
  usecase "Make Payment" as UC_Make
  usecase "Complete Checkout" as UC_Checkout
  usecase "Request Refund" as UC_Refund
  usecase "Create Merchant Account" as UC_CreateAcct
  usecase "Configure Simulation Rules" as UC_SimRules
  usecase "View Payment Status" as UC_Status
  usecase "View Transactions" as UC_ViewTx
  usecase "Generate API Keys" as UC_GenKeys
  usecase "Manage API Keys" as UC_ManageKeys
  usecase "Cancel Payment" as UC_Cancel
  usecase "Configure Webhooks" as UC_Webhooks
  usecase "View System Logs" as UC_Logs
  usecase "Manage Merchants" as UC_ManageMerch
  usecase "Inspect Transaction History" as UC_History

  UC_Make ..> UC_Checkout : <<include>>
  UC_Status ..> UC_ViewTx : <<include>>
  UC_ViewTx ..> UC_History : <<include>>
  UC_Refund ..> UC_ViewTx : <<include>>
}

Customer --> UC_Make
Customer --> UC_Checkout
Customer --> UC_Status
Merchant --> UC_CreateAcct
Merchant --> UC_Refund
Merchant --> UC_SimRules
Merchant --> UC_ViewTx
Merchant --> UC_ManageKeys
Admin --> UC_Cancel
Admin --> UC_Webhooks
Admin --> UC_Logs
Admin --> UC_ManageMerch
Admin --> UC_SimRules
Admin --> UC_GenKeys
Bank --> UC_Make
Notify --> UC_Webhooks

note bottom
  All flows are SIMULATED (TEST MODE).
  No real bank / card network contacted.
  REQ-F-001..080 traceable; see docs/SRS.md
end note
@enduml
